From: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/rockchip: dw-hdmi: RK3528 hot-plug mirrored again at detect

The RK3528 mirrors its HPD GPIO into the VO GRF sink-detect bit at probe,
right after enabling the pad's input, and again only on a GPIO edge. A
screen attached at boot was read as absent on a box and never corrected:
no edge followed. Mirror the level again each time hot-plug is read.

Signed-off-by: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
---
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/dw_hdmi-rockchip.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/dw_hdmi-rockchip.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/dw_hdmi-rockchip.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/dw_hdmi-rockchip.c
@@ -2141,6 +2141,16 @@
 static enum drm_connector_status
 dw_hdmi_rk3528_read_hpd(struct dw_hdmi *dw_hdmi, void *data)
 {
+	struct rockchip_hdmi *hdmi = (struct rockchip_hdmi *)data;
+	u32 val;
+
+	/* the level mirrored at probe can predate the pad's input path */
+	if (hdmi->hpd_gpiod) {
+		val = gpiod_get_value(hdmi->hpd_gpiod) ? RK3528_HDMI_SNKDET : 0;
+		regmap_write(hdmi->regmap, RK3528_VO_GRF_HDMI_MASK,
+			     HIWORD_UPDATE(val, RK3528_HDMI_SNKDET));
+	}
+
 	return dw_hdmi_phy_read_hpd(dw_hdmi, data);
 }
 
